.if \n[.g] .mso www.tmac
.TH SDL_JoystickType 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_JoystickType \- An enum of some common joystick types.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_joystick.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef enum SDL_JoystickType
.BI "{
.BI "    SDL_JOYSTICK_TYPE_UNKNOWN,
.BI "    SDL_JOYSTICK_TYPE_GAMEPAD,
.BI "    SDL_JOYSTICK_TYPE_WHEEL,
.BI "    SDL_JOYSTICK_TYPE_ARCADE_STICK,
.BI "    SDL_JOYSTICK_TYPE_FLIGHT_STICK,
.BI "    SDL_JOYSTICK_TYPE_DANCE_PAD,
.BI "    SDL_JOYSTICK_TYPE_GUITAR,
.BI "    SDL_JOYSTICK_TYPE_DRUM_KIT,
.BI "    SDL_JOYSTICK_TYPE_ARCADE_PAD,
.BI "    SDL_JOYSTICK_TYPE_THROTTLE,
.BI "    SDL_JOYSTICK_TYPE_COUNT
.BI "} SDL_JoystickType;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
In some cases, SDL can identify a low-level joystick as being a certain type of device, and will report it through
.BR SDL_GetJoystickType
(or
.BR SDL_GetJoystickTypeForID )\[char46]
.PP
This is by no means a complete list of everything that can be plugged into a computer\[char46]
.PP
You may refer to
.URL https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/xinput/xinput-and-controller-subtypes "XInput Controller Types"
table for a general understanding of each joystick type\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This enum is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

